      "description": "Core algorithmic techniques, complexity analysis, and data structure tradeoffs.",
      "weight": 1.1,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "al-001",
          "text": "Explain the difference between an array and a linked list.",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "expects": ["contiguous memory", "pointers", "traversal"]
        },
        {
          "id": "al-002",
          "text": "What is a hash map and why is lookup usually constant time?",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "expects": ["hashing", "buckets", "average case"]
        },
        {
          "id": "al-003",
          "text": "Explain the time complexity of a binary search.",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "expects": ["logarithmic", "sorted input"]
        },
        {
          "id": "al-004",
          "text": "How would you find the most frequent element in a list?",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "expects": ["hashmap", "counting", "linear time"]
        },
        {
          "id": "al-005",
          "text": "What is recursion and what are the risks of using it?",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "expects": ["base case", "call stack", "stack overflow"]
        },
        {
          "id": "al-006",
          "text": "Explain how quicksort works and its average-case complexity.",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "expects": ["pivot", "partitioning", "divide and conquer"]
        },
        {
          "id": "al-007",
          "text": "How would you detect a cycle in a linked list?",
